e Omkar mantra; Satyam—the ultimate truth;\nDakshayani—the daughters of Daksha; Dharmapatni—widowed wives; Som—to the Moon God; Kashyapayoh—and to the sage Kashyapa; Api—\nBhi—to the Ganges; Saraswatim—to the Saraswati River; Nandam—to the Nanda River; Kalindi—to the Yamuna River; Sita—\nVarnam—to the Airavata elephant; Dhruvam—to the Dhruva Maharaj; Brahma-rishin—the great sages; sapta—seven; punya-shlokan—\nExtremely pure; and—and; human—to humans; Uththaya—rising up; Apar-Ratra-Ante—At the end of the night; Prayatah—extremely;\nBeing vigilant; Su-Samahitah—with concentration; Smaranti—remembering; Mama—mine; Rupani—to forms; Muchyante—are released;\nare; They—such men; Ahamsa—from the fruits of sinful deeds; Akhilaat—of all kinds..\n\nGod said: Those who are free from the fruits of all sinful deeds, who wake up in the morning after the night\npasses, very carefully their minds in the form of me, your form,\nthis lake, this mountain, caves, gardens, bamboo trees, bamboo trees, Kalpataru, my, Brahma\nand the abodes of Shiva, the three peaks of Trikut mountain made of gold, silver and iron, my"}]}